    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Blue River Provincial Park\"\nsubtitle: \"Permanent plot · Grande Terre, New Caledonia\"\n---\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div id=\"htmlwidget-335af8f6fbac7ff85fa3\" style=\"width:100%;height:367px;\" class=\"leaflet html-widget\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-335af8f6fbac7ff85fa3\">{\"x\":{\"options\":{\"minZoom\":3,\"crs\":{\"crsClass\":\"L.CRS.EPSG3857\",\"code\":null,\"proj4def\":null,\"projectedBounds\":null,\"options\":{}}},\"calls\":[{\"method\":\"addProviderTiles\",\"args\":[\"Esri.WorldGrayCanvas\",null,\"Map\",{\"errorTileUrl\":\"\",\"noWrap\":false,\"detectRetina\":false}]},{\"method\":\"addProviderTiles\",\"args\":[\"Esri.WorldImagery\",null,\"Satellite\",{\"errorTileUrl\":\"\",\"noWrap\":false,\"detectRetina\":false}]},{\"method\":\"addCircleMarkers\",\"args\":[[-20.727398,-22.10677311,-21.6119184,-19.385234,-7.88488,-18.077995],[167.090406,166.68812588,165.7468984,169.294602,157.127126,178.430887],7,null,null,{\"interactive\":true,\"className\":\"\",\"stroke\":true,\"color\":\"#16262B\",\"weight\":1,\"opacity\":0.5,\"fill\":true,\"fillColor\":\"#C98A1B\",\"fillOpacity\":0.6},null,null,[\"<b>Siloam<\\/b><br>Lifou, New Caledonia<br><a href='../plots/siloam.html'>More &rarr;<\\/a>\",\"<b>Blue River Provincial Park<\\/b><br>Grande Terre, New Caledonia<br><a href='../plots/blue-river.html'>More &rarr;<\\/a>\",\"<b>Great Ferns Provincial Park<\\/b><br>Grande Terre, New Caledonia<br><a href='../plots/great-ferns.html'>More &rarr;<\\/a>\",\"<b>Nusumetu<\\/b><br>Tanna, Vanuatu<br><a href='../plots/nusumetu.html'>More &rarr;<\\/a>\",\"<b>Poitete<\\/b><br>Kolombangara, Solomon Islands<br><a href='../plots/poitete.html'>More &rarr;<\\/a>\",\"<b>Vago<\\/b><br>Viti Levu, Fiji<br><a href='../plots/vago.html'>More &rarr;<\\/a>\"],null,null,{\"interactive\":false,\"permanent\":false,\"direction\":\"auto\",\"opacity\":1,\"offset\":[0,0],\"textsize\":\"10px\",\"textOnly\":false,\"className\":\"\",\"sticky\":true},null]},{\"method\":\"addLayersControl\",\"args\":[[\"Map\",\"Satellite\"],[],{\"collapsed\":false,\"autoZIndex\":true,\"position\":\"topright\"}]},{\"method\":\"addLegend\",\"args\":[{\"colors\":[\"#C98A1B\"],\"labels\":[\"Permanent plots\"],\"na_color\":null,\"na_label\":\"NA\",\"opacity\":1,\"position\":\"bottomleft\",\"type\":\"unknown\",\"title\":null,\"extra\":null,\"layerId\":null,\"className\":\"info legend\",\"group\":null}]}],\"limits\":{\"lat\":[-22.10677311,-7.88488],\"lng\":[157.127126,178.430887]},\"setView\":[[-22.10677311,166.68812588],9,[]]},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n\n|                       |                                                                                                                         |\n|:----------------------|:------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n|Country                |New Caledonia                                                                                                            |\n|Island                 |Grande Terre                                                                                                             |\n|Latitude               |-22.1068                                                                                                                 |\n|Longitude              |166.6881                                                                                                                 |\n|Elevation (approx.)    |180 m                                                                                                                    |\n|Substrate              |Ultramafic (peridotite)                                                                                                  |\n|Established            |March 2025                                                                                                               |\n|Principal investigator |Thomas Ibanez (Research Fellow, UMR AMAP, French National Research Institute for Sustainable Development, New Caledonia) |\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Description\n\nThe Blue River permanent plot lies in the Blue River Provincial Park, on an alluvial flat with ultramafic soils in the south of the island of Grande Terre. The park is managed by the South Province. The plot was set up in March 2025 at about 180 m elevation and resurveyed in March 2026. The forest was logged until the late 1950s and has been protected since 1980. It still shows traces of past logging, as well as a large gap probably created by a tropical storm or cyclone.\n\nThe most abundant tree species are *Codia jaffrei* (Cunoniaceae), *Archidendropsis granulosa* (Fabaceae) and *Plerandra gabriellae* (Araliaceae). The largest and tallest tree is a *Didymocheton rufescens* (Meliaceae).\n\nThe plot lies within a larger 90 ha canopy observatory that is regularly surveyed by drone as part of the [CanObs](https://canobs.net/riviere-bleue-observatory) project.\n\n## Field team\n\nDavid Bruy, Coline Cavagnet, Julie Dibon, Manon Durand, Nathan Eltabet, Patrick Heuret, Thomas Ibanez, Vaea Lefeuvre, Chrystelle Nigote, Emmanuelle Vanhalle and Ghislain Vieilledent.\n\n[← All permanent plots](../plots.qmd) · [Network map](../index.qmd)\n",
